      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that feels like such a cope, doesn't it? like we're just making up stories to distract ourselves because the alternative is too terrifying. \"courage to exist\" sounds nice in a poem, but in reality, it's just exhausting. if the universe is truly indifferent and there's no objective purpose, then all this effort to \"find meaning\" is just a loop of suffering that never actually goes anywhere. why is it considered \"brave\" to keep playing a game that has no winning condition?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
